WEBVTT

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.950
We did it! It worked.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.910
Congratulations, Professor!

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.820
The Moon Hall exists after all.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.080
It may only happen once every few centuries, but it's here!

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.040
It's a beautiful planet...

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.920
Professor! The Moon Hall is...

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:30.800
Do not worry.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:36.590
If we use the space-time selector to go slightly into the past, we can return using the same Moon Hall.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:38.510
I expect nothing less from you, Professor!

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:45.690
What happened?!

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.190
The engine is malfunctioning!

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.940
Oh, no! We're going to crash!

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:53.440
Hurry up and get in!

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.030
No, you get in, Professor!

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:55.860
Just get in!

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:57.700
I can't! You get in!

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.800
It's been an honor, Professor.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.130
Please, be well.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:16.130
Har—

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.550
That's the story.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:01.640
I feel like I'm going crazy

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:07.390
I like nice songs

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:11.860
and I want you to listen to them too

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:16.820
Whenever

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:22.490
I sing a song

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:26.080
I hear a voice coming from the microphone

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.500
wishing me the best

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.250
I want you

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:32.790
to hear it too

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:33.630
Good luck!

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.800
You can't show your love

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:43.300
just with niceties

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:48.180
That won't provide comfort

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.560
Whenever I say something

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.650
out of the ordinary

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.950
in my heart

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.450
I wish you the best

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.990
I want you

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:08.620
to hear that line

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:09.620
Good luck!

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:42.990
Ow...

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:47.410
Mom! Practice with me more seriously.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:49.240
Don't rush, Momo.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.540
You'll leave more openings.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.330
I want to become strong!

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.460
I see you've awaken, peach thief.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:02.920
Ugh, where am I?

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:06.010
This is the home of master fencer, Fujiwara Haru!

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:14.560
You should be thankful that we didn't hand you over to the vigilante squad.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:18.980
Sorry, but those peaches were super delicious!

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:22.360
Of course they were. My mom grew them!

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:25.740
Peach farmer, huh? Must be why your name means "peach"!

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:29.660
My name is Hibiki Ai. Nice to meet you!

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.210
Why were you wandering around there?

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:38.500
Oh, I'm on a journey to train.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.340
I want to be a Best. A drifter Best!

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:43.840
A drifter Best? Impossible.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:47.970
No Best is as bad as you were yesterday.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:50.760
That's because I'm still training.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.980
Besides, to become a Best, I need a...

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.980
Hey, Haru!

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:59.520
Oh, what a darling thief.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:01.530
I'm glad we made it in time for breakfast.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.240
Here, eat as much as you'd like.

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:07.240
Thanks!

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.320
We should help each other in times of need.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:11.950
We owe a lot to Haru.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:15.120
Don't think your transgression has been forgiven.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.250
You'll make up for it in labor.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.670
S'rry...

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:25.010
I'm heading to school, Mom!

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:27.260
There've been a lot of school days recently, huh?

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:29.390
See you later!

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.270
The tax collector!

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.270
We don't have any money! Go away!

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.770
If you refuse to pay your taxes,

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:41.770
then I must use force.

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:43.900
I'd like to see you try!

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:46.780
Momo!

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.030
Here's this month's taxes.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:55.540
Thank you.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.130
Don't do anything stupid.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:01.170
But...

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:05.590
What were you going to do after you drove him away?

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.640
Momo, the dog! The dog!

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:11.760
Chi...

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:14.560
What was that, anyway?

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:16.730
The tax collector for the Okayama Demons.

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:18.810
He's the demon's pawn.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.150
Demon?

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:27.740
Here in Okayama, the state vigilante squad captain manages the tax system.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:30.990
She has us pay far more than other nations.

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:36.870
The captain, Kukino Ura, used to be beloved by the nation.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.330
Aren't you strong, though?

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.130
You should take her down a peg!

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:47.460
C-Can you explain that one more time?

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:49.380
I've already been over it five times.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:50.760
U-Um...

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:54.010
It's coming soon.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:07:02.020
Every 415 years, there comes a night when the two moons touch.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:05.270
The Extreme Double Super Moon.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:10.280
On that night, I must bring that girl back to her home planet.

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:13.700
The girl I got involved...

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:18.200
Are you saying you're an... ali—

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:22.420
I don't care what planet you're from,

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:26.250
but is it true that my Otonashi was the one kidnapped?

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:27.550
It appears to be.

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:29.760
This is what the enemy said:

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:33.470
"If you value the life of the girl who claims to be the president's daughter,

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:36.220
then bring out the eighth
octopus-pot-shaped engine unit."

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:38.600
Where is it?

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:39.430
I don't know...

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:41.430
You've got to be kidding me.

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:42.810
Octopus pot?

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:50.150
It's been missing ever since I got the ship from the display at Aviation Park after becoming president.

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.570
I-Is that a UFO?!

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:57.410
The enemy is the gang without honor and humanity that controls Hiroshima.

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:59.790
We can't expect honest negotiations.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:04.330
Retrieve the stolen Cores, the seven octopus pots,

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:05.960
and the girl whose hat this is.

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.670
Octopus pots...

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:11.260
We can't do much without our stones, though.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:12.840
Do you want a protective charm?

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:18.140
Even Bests need more than just time to recuperate, huh?

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:20.600
What's this?

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.310
Octopus pots...

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:24.390
Exhibition
Historical
Tokorozawa
Mystery of the Octopus
Pot in the Land with no Sea
Mystery of the Octopus
Pot in the Land with no Sea

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:28.860
What?!

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:31.280
I should have noticed sooner!

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:34.360
Weren't you the designer's assistant?

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:36.410
I was still a student then,

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:38.910
and a pretty bad assistant.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.450
There has been a change of plans!

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:50.130
Yukina!

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:54.130
She's not nearby!

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:55.630
Let's widen our search area!

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.140
R-Right!

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:03.180
Thank you very much. You saved me.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:04.980
Don't fall on your way back.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.390
I won't.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:22.120
This is...

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.500
Good work, Otomo.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:30.840
My apologies for failing to retrieve them all.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.010
So, we need one more octopus pot.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.390
I'm sure the president of Tokorozawa

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:49.480
would happily trade it for her dear daughter.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:01.450
<i>I think she's...</i>

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:02.490
<i>This person's...</i>

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:04.330
<i>From Hiyoshicho Propellers...</i>

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.620
<i>Been caught for doing something bad, huh?</i>

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.670
Hey, wait! Don't you know who I am?

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:13.840
Wait, I know you can hear me!

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:15.840
The picture is different?

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:17.800
Aren't they just sisters or something?

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:20.430
Wouldn't she put up pictures of both of them, then?

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:22.510
It's fine as long as they're involved somehow.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.520
<i>Miss Chiaya's been taken hostage?</i>

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.850
<i>And something's been stolen from the office?</i>

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:32.980
<i>Calm down. I need to prioritize.</i>

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:37.610
Hey, Fatcho!

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:39.400
The hell is this?
Missing Person

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:40.610
D-Dunno...
Missing Person

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:42.200
Wait, Miss?!

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.990
Now that I've had a good look at you,

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.870
you're not Fatcho.

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:58.480
Why did you wake up the guard?

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:01.430
I couldn't just let you steal the key.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.970
Mr. Momiyama?

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:14.190
So, you can't get a hold of that Momiyama person?

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:18.650
No, and he's never missed a check-in call.

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:21.320
Can we really fight with these?

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:24.450
I think it has more practical use than a lucky charm.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.330
Huh?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:31.080
Um, will Nozomi be eaten up by that Chiaya girl?

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:35.590
I didn't eat you, did I?

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:38.210
Well then, please follow the plan.

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:47.680
Haru, the Mimasaka Peaches have decided to exterminate the ogres.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.890
I don't think anyone still remembers how to do that.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.770
Th-That might be true, but... you know.

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:54.480
Yeah...

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:58.690
Okayama Demons' Kukino Ura is no ordinary Best.

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:05.200
We know that. She protected Okayama from Hiroshima's Ishizukuri Stones in the past.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:06.070
Haru, actually—

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:07.080
Not now.

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:12.290
I know you're still fretting about burying Tottori in sand,

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:15.580
but that battle was also to protect Okayama.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:17.670
Please protect everyone one more time.

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:20.380
Sorry, but I must refuse.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:24.800
We may be poor, but Momo and I are living a peaceful life.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:29.390
As long as we don't ask for much, living in this country isn't bad.

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:30.470
Haru...

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:33.520
Ai. Do you understand how to do it now?

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:35.230
Uh, kinda...

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:36.900
I'm off to make door-to-door sales.

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:39.690
Get them all harvested before sundown.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:41.440
All of them?!

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:54.330
Find her?

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:59.170
I have come for the state vigilante squad license.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:03.800
I said we would withdraw, but I didn't say we would hand over the license.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:06.260
I will carry it to the grave with me.

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:10.350
I have always respected you as a member of the main family.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.640
Please step down gracefully.

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:15.520
Who cares about a flimsy piece of paper with writing on it?

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:16.810
While there's still fire in my—

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:20.690
Allow me to extinguish that fire.

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:25.450
I'm afraid you'll have to enter your grave empty-handed.

